The TypeScript adaptation keeps the C float types of filter_flt (factor, gain
and param as float, every float operation rounded with Math.fround, no
contraction) and the double arithmetic of filter_dbl. It implements only
oversample=1, so get_lowpass and run_lowpassf/run_lowpassd are not adapted, and
it refuses the tanh, atan, cubic, exp, quintic, sin and erf types, oversampling,
timeline enable, runtime commands and non-finite input instead of approximating
them. It adds no FFmpeg runtime code. The original source and full notices
remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
